From aba855b434a4034961bbcbe7cda83b3dbbf175c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:46:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Read and write the Go60's MoErgo JSON

The MoErgo JSON codec knew one board: an 80-key Glove80 table into a
6x14 matrix. A Go60 layout stopped at "expected 'glove80'", although the
TOML model, the go60-rmk board and its key map already describe it.

moergo/board.rs names both boards: the Go60's editor-to-matrix table
(taken from crates/go60-rmk/keyboard.toml's map, the matrix transform of
MoErgo's go60.dtsi), rows, thumbs and halves. Import picks the board
from the document's keyboard field (or its layer length), export from
the snapshot's shape, and a template for the other board is refused.
Go60 layers of 62 entries (the trackpad slots some exports add) are read
past; 60 are written. Bilateral hold-taps get the Go60's other half and
thumbs as trigger positions.

Import also accepts ZMK's short PSCRN and SLCK, which the Go60 factory
layout uses.

Tests: MoErgo's Go60 factory default imports with nothing dropped, its
keys land on the cells the board map names, and it round-trips to the
same snapshot with and without itself as template, keeping its
trackpad listeners.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
